Subject: [PATCH v2 0/2] regulator: wl2868c: add the WL2868C camera PMIC

This series adds support for the Will Semiconductor WL2868C, a
seven-channel I2C camera PMIC found on the Lenovo Legion Tab (TB322FC,
SM8750).

Patch 1 is the DT binding. It is a verbatim resend of the v2 posted on
its own earlier today as

  <20261028120442.99375-1-xiaqinghuan@mail.ustc.edu.cn>

which already carries the fixes from the v1 review (regulator-first
subject prefix, MAINTAINERS entry sorted into the W section, no
linux-media list, consumer description). It is repeated here only so
the series is complete and bisectable: submitting-patches.rst asks for
the Documentation/ part to come before the code implementing the
binding, and the devicetree submitting-patches.rst asks for the binding
to be kept with the driver that uses it. Reviewers who already looked
at patch 1 need not look at it again.

Patch 2 is the driver itself, which is also the answer to the review
question about whether this was premature: the binding was posted ahead
of the driver, the driver exists, and it has a real consumer on the
board named in the binding.

Consumer, from the TB322FC device tree:

  - rear camera, samsung,s5kjns: dvdd -> LDO1, avdd -> LDO4,
    dovdd -> LDO7
  - front camera, galaxycore,gc08a8: dvdd -> LDO2, avdd -> LDO3,
    dovdd -> LDO7
  - rear VCM, giantec,gt9764: vdd -> LDO5, vddio -> LDO7

So LDO1 to LDO5 and LDO7 are all in use; LDO6 is the only unused
output.

The driver is a plain regulator driver: regmap over I2C, one
regulator_desc per LDO registered with devm_regulator_register(), linear
voltage mapping, and no private sysfs or debugfs interface. SYS_EN, the
chip-wide enable bit, is set and checked together with the per-LDO bit
because no output comes up without it.

